{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems","id":925797,"title":"Uncommon Lunar totems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-04T02:08:24-07:00","id":925797,"title":"Uncommon Lunar totems","content":"Some totems are quite common (felines, canines, tyrant lizards, etc.), either because they're badass, or because they have well-known symbolism.<br /> For your PCs or NPCs needs, here's a bunch of more unusual ideas (either lesser-known species or popular ones with interesting abilities), that are lesser known but cool, have interesting behaviours or abilities, or mythological significance.<br /> <br /> - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower_mantis\" target=\"_blank\">Mantises</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hornet_moth\" target=\"_blank\">moths</a>, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Misumena_vatia\" target=\"_blank\">spiders</a> that mimic flowers or other arthropod species. Great for seductive/appealing killers and spies.<br /> - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diving_bell_spider\" target=\"_blank\">Diving bell spiders</a> are unusual underwater predators, using large air bubbles for many purposes. Think about it when you've got games involving large bodies of water.<br /> - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_raven\" target=\"_blank\">Corvids</a>. Alright, they're not really underused, but what's lesser-known is their huge sociability and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tool_use_by_animals\" target=\"_blank\">tool-making prowess</a>. It goes far enough that clans of crows might make tools with similar purpose but different appearance or fabrication means, and pass down the technique to their descendants, making it something that we might call a tradition.<br /> - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elephant\" target=\"_blank\">Elephants</a> are also well-known, especially for their intelligence and memory. They would make great fit for any occult/mystical-oriented Lunar due to their <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elephant_cognition#Death_ritual\" target=\"_blank\">death rituals</a> and high sociability (young elephants, mostly males, whose parents were poached when they were little, having grown up without proper socialization, grow to be aggressive, awkward, even vengeful, adults, which in turn can be passed down to their own children; a phenomenon observed sometimes among humans).<br /> - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electroreception\" target=\"_blank\">Sharks and rays</a> (and also platypi, who get weirder at every new fact learnt about them) perceive the electromagnetic field of living beings, and hunt or flee accordingly.<br /> - Ants practice <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slave-making_ant\" target=\"_blank\">slavery</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leafcutter_ant\" target=\"_blank\">agriculture</a> and [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aphid#Mutualism] (aphid) husbandry. You can build civilizations with that!<br /> - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarantula_hawk\" target=\"_blank\">Tarantula hawks</a>, unlike their name indicates, are wasps. They do hunt tarantulas much bigger than them, and their sting is immensely painful. Great for a hunter of monsters and behemoths.<br /> - There's little to add about dolphins, besides that they're not the species one usually thinks about first when looking for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolphin\" target=\"_blank\">seemingly pointless or cruel aggressiveness</a>. Paradoxically, it might be a great fit for a sociopathic character.<br /> - Dogs. Bear with me for a second. While domesticated by humans, they also pretty much domesticated themselves to improve relations with humans, to the point of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Origin_of_the_domestic_dog#Convergent_evolution_between_dogs_and_humans\" target=\"_blank\">learning to understand them</a> and live with them. That's adaptability right there.<br /> - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bombardier_beetle\" target=\"_blank\">Bombardier beetles</a>. They throw explosives at your face. 'nuff said.<br /> - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bigfin_squid\" target=\"_blank\">Bigfin squids</a>, while not very well understood even by scientists, have the merit of being damn creepy and huge.<br /> <br /> <br /> Will add more later! Feel free to add your own ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T03:51:13-07:00","id":925817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems#post925797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Ants practice <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slave-making_ant\" target=\"_blank\">slavery</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leafcutter_ant\" target=\"_blank\">agriculture</a> and [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aphid#Mutualism] (aphid) husbandry. You can build civilizations with that!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think humans already know how to do those things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've lately been thinking about the image of a Lunar whose other form is a sheep. Not wild species of sheep, mind, the domestic sheep. A kind of mixture of that image of placidity and fierce protectiveness.<br /> <br /> Also zebras; zebras are vicious. There's a reason humans had to reach Asia before they found equines that could be domesticated.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T04:47:48-07:00","id":925823,"title":"","content":"Mantis shrimp and pistol shrimp. One for punching, one for gun...ching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T05:19:40-07:00","id":925830,"title":"","content":"Last edition I made an albatross-totem Lunar who didn't see much play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T08:07:53-07:00","id":925901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=925823#post925823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mantis shrimp and pistol shrimp. One for punching, one for gun...ching.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot about the spring-loaded cutting blades. Watch your fingers and toes underwater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T08:34:19-07:00","id":925912,"title":"","content":"I've got a concept floating around somewhere for a Swan-totem lunar. Poised, elegant, and will flip out and start bludgeoning people to death with her bare hands at the drop of a hat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11863-jondera","name":"Jondera","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T09:41:12-07:00","id":925937,"title":"","content":"A seagul-totem'd lunar, as a western lunar. Just as an alternative to all the other generic bird-totem'd lunars<br /> <br /> A mole totem'd lunar: round, stocky, likes to dig and such. Perhaps an unappetising taste for eating raw worms?<br /> <br /> A... ok, in the core book there's a monster/beast entry for some giant eastern bug that lays its eggs in people who are still alive. That, as a totem. Would make for some really messy interrogation tactics...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T10:02:28-07:00","id":925945,"title":"","content":"Animals worth checking out in creation:<br /> <br /> -Blackstar Mastiffs (bonus point, being so smart means you can pass for a blackstar mastiff without arousing suspicion, even better favored hound of the realm.)<br /> -Crag Cat<br /> -Emperor Rat<br /> -Giant Rats<br /> -Giant Spiders<br /> -Grelidaka<br /> -griefbees<br /> -Hearth-cat<br /> -Ichneumon Hunter (the bugs <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar588_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"588\" data-vbnamecard=\"588\">webkilla</a> mentioned)<br /> -Mammoths<br /> -Scarlet Crane<br /> -Tongma Monkeys<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T10:15:22-07:00","id":925952,"title":"","content":"Starfish/Seacucumber - lots of lovecraftian themes (wait you turn you stomach inside out of your mouth to digest things?) plus massive regeneration. In one game had it produce small clones (extras) whenever it took damage.<br /> <br /> Honey Guide, bird that leads Honey Badgers and Humans to bee hives and feeds on the larvae when it is busted open. Works really well as in a support role with a partner that doesn't give a fuck. <br /> <br /> Irukandji jellyfish, tiny jelly (less then an inch) with three foot thread like tentacles. Deadly and mindnumbingly painful. So painful morphine does not help. Good for a ninja/assassin.<br /> <br /> Issus Leafhooper, aside from insanely fast jumping and acceleration they are the first example of an animal that uses gears to keep its legs in synch. Could work for a steampunk crafter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T10:29:31-07:00","id":925960,"title":"","content":"<b>Star Nosed Mole.</b> Star Nosed Moles have one of the most impressive sensory organs of any animal in the world. They are theorized to hunt by sensing the electrical fields of their prey, and it's known that its brain works at an incredible quickly - it can identify food in less than 8 milliseconds, which is many times faster than any other discovered animal. Further, it's an insanely fast eater as it can identify and eat many types of food in less than 120 milliseconds - in comparison it takes about 350 milliseconds for the average human to blink.<br /> <br /> <b>Giant Isopod </b> Giant Isopods have natural armor and their stamina is amazing - they can go for over five years without eating anything and still be perfectly healthy. They're also largely immune to pressure, being able to survive miles beneath the surface of the ocean and at sea level with no ill effects. And, while they're typically scavengers, they're also scary as fuck predators - there was a video on a recent Shark Week of a giant isopod latching onto a much larger dog shark and killing it by <i>eating through its face</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T10:39:01-07:00","id":925969,"title":"","content":"Wombat for a Full Moon. Because if you're going to play a combat wombat, you might as well play a /combat wombat/. Seriously, wombats are noted for treating fences as minor obstacles to be gone under or /through/. And unlike most burrowing animals, they have armour plating on their rumps. They aren't terribly aggressive, but they're ridiculously strong and tough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T11:27:48-07:00","id":925993,"title":"","content":"Raccoon for an alternative to rodent/corvid trickster and tool-use archetypes. Otters work great here for something more light-hearted. I always thought playing a Boar totem Lunar would be neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T12:15:18-07:00","id":926017,"title":"","content":"Centipedes are probably used far less than spiders.<br /> <br /> Also, anything bioluminescent, which gives the option of the Tell being some form of bioluminescence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T12:20:25-07:00","id":926019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=925937#post925937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A... ok, in the core book there's a monster/beast entry for some giant eastern bug that lays its eggs in people who are still alive. That, as a totem. Would make for some really messy interrogation tactics...</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone at a game I was in went with that, my reaction would be... Um... Pretty much Doug's here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ldSwwVMllyE?t=9\" data-code=\"ldSwwVMllyE\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ldSwwVMllyE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> Yeah, stuff like that is very much in the Do Not Want territory for me.<br /> <br /> On the original topic... Octopus! They're clever, they're talented, and their innate squishiness, ability to slip through small openings, and their ability to change color to match their surroundings makes them surprisingly skilled spies and assassins!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T13:29:23-07:00","id":926055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=925817#post925817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think humans already know how to do those things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, when you put it this way... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I do think it brings another dimension to the practice, though. That's a great justification for a civilized Lunar, though one pushing their own vision of it (with weird personal definitions of slavery, agriculture, animal husbandry, ....).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:01:30-07:00","id":926065,"title":"","content":"I've said it before and I'll say it again. The lunar with a chicken totem has a lot of areas where it can blend in without raising suspicion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:02:09-07:00","id":926066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=925937#post925937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A seagul-totem'd lunar, as a western lunar. Just as an alternative to <b>all the other generic bird-totem'd lunars</b></div> </div> </div> </div>What's &quot;generic&quot; about an albatross?!?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:11:24-07:00","id":926074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926065#post926065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said it before and I'll say it again. The lunar with a chicken totem has a lot of areas where it can blend in without raising suspicion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, something about being perfectly able to survive without (most of) their head!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:12:57-07:00","id":926076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926055#post926055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, when you put it this way... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I do think it brings another dimension to the practice, though. That's a great justification for a civilized Lunar, though one pushing their own vision of it (with weird personal definitions of slavery, agriculture, animal husbandry, ....).</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI think it's more the other way around; the Lunar with that kind of personality might express it as an ant totem, but turning into an ant is not itself going to help do those kinds of things, and Lunar Charms are probably not going to be as fixated on their totem as all that.<br /> <br /> First and foremost, Lunars need to be Lunars, not four hundred vaguely associated Chosen of different animals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:16:24-07:00","id":926081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926076#post926076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI think it's more the other way around; the Lunar with that kind of personality might express it as an ant totem, but turning into an ant is not itself going to help do those kinds of things, and Lunar Charms are probably not going to be as fixated on their totem as all that.<br /> <br /> First and foremost, Lunars need to be Lunars, not four hundred vaguely associated Chosen of different animals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That said, a system by which a Lunar can make evocations for their forms instead of for their weapons would be kinda neat. Not huge spanning charm trees, but 5-6 little evocations that run off the 'themes' of an animal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:20:40-07:00","id":926083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926081#post926081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, a system by which a Lunar can make evocations for their forms instead of for their weapons would be kinda neat. Not huge spanning charm trees, but 5-6 little evocations that run off the 'themes' of an animal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually a very nice idea! It would allow you to have a generic slate of Charms for Lunars so that Lunars could be Lunars, while allowing players to make a handful of unique widgets that reflect their own totem animal. You wouldn't have very many of those Evocation-type Charms, so they would tend to serve more as flavor for a Lunar than as the basic chassis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:21:48-07:00","id":926084,"title":"","content":"The weirdest totems I had encountered in past editions were:<br /> Fainting Goat<br /> Parrot (Pirate-themed lunar)<br /> Human (Lunar was actually one of the sentient cats in Halta)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T16:09:13-07:00","id":926129,"title":"","content":"<u>Two I've used</u><br /> <br /> <b>Guinea pig/cavy</b> - Great for a scientific No-Moon who relies on social skills rather than ferocity. A sweet, bumbling, slightly <i>zaftig</i> woman. Her anima was moonlight between the bars of a wireframe cage and the soft crunch of bedding underfoot<br /> <b>Rabbit</b> - Read Watership Down. Rabbits are fucking badass, and El Ahrairah is the iconic Lunar trickster. Make great messengers, skirmishers, and scouts. I've got a courier named Nu Zayets Pogodi (if you get that reference, you get 10,000 Soviet Rubles) who was my answer to weird manga bunnygirl fapbait: A tall, rangy, woman with legs that could kick your head in and a keen, thin, clever face. She kept her ears tied back when not in use. Yes, her tell was an adorable fluffy tail. There's only so Social Justicey even I can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11816,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","user":"Foxcalibur","date":".  Changed fapbat to fapbait. Not that the rare Ahn-Tengese fapbat wouldn't be an awesome totem. 07-04-2016, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T16:33:04-07:00","id":926147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926065#post926065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said it before and I'll say it again. The lunar with a chicken totem has a lot of areas where it can blend in without raising suspicion.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;That one is not a chicken.&quot;<br /> <br /> Overheard during a conversation between the Birdman, Kahlan and Richard from The Sword of Truth Series, by Terry Goodkind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T17:03:31-07:00","id":926171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926065#post926065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said it before and I'll say it again. The lunar with a chicken totem has a lot of areas where it can blend in without raising suspicion.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=45bUOIK2cAo\" data-code=\"45bUOIK2cAo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/45bUOIK2cAo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T18:05:41-07:00","id":926189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wick Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926147#post926147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;That one is not a chicken.&quot;<br /> <br /> Overheard during a conversation between the Birdman, Kahlan and Richard from The Sword of Truth Series, by Terry Goodkind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, c'mon! You gotta put in the full line for maximum lulz!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Soul of Fire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The bird let out a slow chicken cackle. It sounded like a chicken, but in her heart she knew it wasn't. In that instant, she completely understood the concept of a chicken that was not a chicken. This looked like a chicken, like most of the Mud People's chickens. But this was no chicken. This was evil manifest.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T18:07:12-07:00","id":926190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926171#post926171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahaha! That's so funny!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T21:42:03-07:00","id":926267,"title":"","content":"Speaking of chickens, consider the Ayam Cemani, native to Indonesia. It's a chicken that is black from comb to claw. It's amazing.<br /> <br /> You know what I don't see much of? Grasshopper Lunars. You'd think somebody somewhere was a Kamen Rider fan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T22:20:22-07:00","id":926279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926267#post926267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of chickens, consider the Ayam Cemani, native to Indonesia. It's a chicken that is black from comb to claw. It's amazing.<br /> <br /> You know what I don't see much of? Grasshopper Lunars. You'd think somebody somewhere was a Kamen Rider fan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totem size restrictions and all. Ants, grasshoppers, flies, and numerous others are, with overwhelming frequency, smaller than the size of a field mouse, and thus have typically not been available as totems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T23:08:14-07:00","id":926288,"title":"","content":"I generally assume &quot;It's Creation, there's going to be a giant something somewhere&quot; when it comes to very small things. I mean, the real world already has centipedes a foot long, and Creation still has megafauna, so I imagine that somewhere, there's more or less every sort of bug in a horrible, horrible size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T00:23:05-07:00","id":926306,"title":"","content":"You mean <a href=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/witcher/images/4/41/The_Scolopendromorph_--_its_harder_to_kill_than_to_pronounce_its_name.png/revision/latest?cb=20160424205742\" target=\"_blank\">scolopendromorph</a>? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T03:46:39-07:00","id":926351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926306#post926306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean <a href=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/witcher/images/4/41/The_Scolopendromorph_--_its_harder_to_kill_than_to_pronounce_its_name.png/revision/latest?cb=20160424205742\" target=\"_blank\">scolopendromorph</a>? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I am thinking <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/5c/b7/0d/5cb70d6fa6079ef37cf6b829821d63ea.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Arthropleura</i> </a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T06:50:13-07:00","id":926380,"title":"","content":"The two I was happiest with were Buffalo and Cicada. The latter would leave a silvery exuvia for a few second any time he changed shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T06:55:52-07:00","id":926381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MuscaDomestica</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926351#post926351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I am thinking <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/5c/b7/0d/5cb70d6fa6079ef37cf6b829821d63ea.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Arthropleura</i> </a></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naked_Lunch_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">Giant Brazilian Aquatic Centipedes!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T07:43:44-07:00","id":926401,"title":"","content":"So, we have prehistoric animals in Creation. That already makes a lot o dinosaurs available. They are specially fresh if you go by the latest more proto-feathery reconstructions (go and google a triceratops).<br /> <br /> But also you may want to include not just creatures from our past in your Creation. Why not use animals from the future? I've created a couple of hypothetical animals similar to those in the future earth documentaries. Some were neat ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T08:01:12-07:00","id":926413,"title":"","content":"I have always want to make a Lunar with this totem.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.mun.ca/biology/scarr/Dixon_Night_Stalker.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T08:05:33-07:00","id":926418,"title":"","content":"I have never seen a bat-totemed Lunar in a game. I'd love to.<br /> <br /> Of course, I second the Octopus suggestion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T08:32:14-07:00","id":926433,"title":"","content":"I just realised that my mock spirit-animal is perfect for a Lunar Totem. Behold, an Exalted of the moon, drawing forth from the vast untapped power of the noble tapeworm! Bureaucracy (because what else fits a vile intestinal parasite?), stealth, and an icky, icky version of Shadow Replacement Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T09:22:28-07:00","id":926457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926076#post926076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI think it's more the other way around; the Lunar with that kind of personality might express it as an ant totem, but turning into an ant is not itself going to help do those kinds of things, and Lunar Charms are probably not going to be as fixated on their totem as all that.<br /> <br /> First and foremost, Lunars need to be Lunars, not four hundred vaguely associated Chosen of different animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so what are Lunars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:23:19-07:00","id":926488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926457#post926457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so what are Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>...hoo, boy. There's a loaded question.<br /> <br /> Lunars, perhaps fittingly, are a lot of different things to a lot of different people. Were I not about to go grab lunch, I'd have more to say about that and where I personally stand. But alas, I am so I don't. Suffice it to say that IMHO the shapeshifting marks the kinds of characters they are intended to be very well, but needn't be core to them.<br /> <br /> Alternately, a miserable pile of shapes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:28:46-07:00","id":926493,"title":"","content":"Seriously though, are Lunar the &quot;Mythical Beast Champion&quot; or &quot;Animal Planet Hero&quot; ? I'm looking at this thread at all I see is the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 07-05-2016, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T12:14:43-07:00","id":926552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926493#post926493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously though, are Lunar the &quot;Mythical Beast Champion&quot; or &quot;Animal Planet Hero&quot; ? I'm looking at this thread at all I see is the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's probably a good reason for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T12:49:48-07:00","id":926573,"title":"","content":"I want to see someone play a Lunar with a Pacman Toad as a totem. Being able to swallow things equal to nearly 50% of their body mass and dimensions would be amusing.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of interesting animals to use for totems that I've yet to see or hear of: poisonous tree frogs, ant-eaters, woodpeckers, snails, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T13:43:32-07:00","id":926607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926493#post926493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously though, are Lunar the &quot;Mythical Beast Champion&quot; or &quot;Animal Planet Hero&quot; ? I'm looking at this thread at all I see is the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've been geeking out almost exclusively about miscellaneous scientific animal facts there. (Not that there's anything bad about it; I've seen the pistol shrimp example pop up remarkably frequently in discussions !)<br /> Very little about mythological animals, so of course this thread includes less of the former. I'll try to provide uncommon animals with their associated myths, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T14:06:46-07:00","id":926621,"title":"","content":"I'd draw the line here:<br /> <br /> If the mythical animal at one point has a stable breeding population (like huge flying hawks), then it isn't a mythical animal in Creation. Go for it, Lunar.<br /> <br /> If the mythical animal is considered a spiritual entity (like dragons) or requires a Sorcererous working to create, then it isn't a valid Lunar Totem. A lunar would need special knacks/charms to take that animal's form. <br /> <br /> I have a friend that wants to play one of the Humans living in Malfeas turned lunar with a demonic totem. That is probably grey area and would need ST judgement to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T14:19:01-07:00","id":926630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926621#post926621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a friend that wants to play one of the Humans living in Malfeas turned lunar with a demonic totem. That is probably grey area and would need ST judgement to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are things in the Brass City that are just strange and unusually beasts - like flying rays or living tents - which could serve as a demon like totem without actually being a demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T17:24:06-07:00","id":926728,"title":"","content":"Going off what I said earlier about beast-form Evocations, I think that would be a good way to turn 'animal planet heroes' into Mythical Beast Heroes. Evocations should be based off themes and myths, so instead of a bear evocation be 'go be a bear', it should be like... <br /> <br /> <br /> The fierce northman lunar sees the Bear as the VIkings did - a terrifying combatant, something that crushes through the enemy, that acted as inspiration for the berserker. They develop evocations based on their belief of what a bear <b>is</b>. Their bear can resist wound penalties, can charge through a battlegroup to get to its commander, can ignore swords sticking into even their heart.<br /> <br /> The Realms-born lunar sees the Bear as Britain did - as Artaois, the legendary warrior and leader, whom's spirit King Arthur carried. They create evocations of glorious leadership, they gain bonuses for being in the thick of battle alongside their allies, they are preternaturally skillful, able hear arrows from ten thousand meters away, and avoid them.<br /> <br /> The Eastern Lunar sees the Bear as Artio, the Guardian Goddess of the Celts irl. They create evocations of protectiveness, they form attachments to their 'cubs' and move to defend them from any blow. She gains strength as her cubs are injured, but does not rush into battle needlessly.<br /> <br /> <br /> All three of these lunars are still a Bear Totem lunar. But all three have their own myths and legends about what a Bear is. The same can be done for many animals, though 'weirder' and more 'modern' animals (such as the ever popular pistol shrimp, which I've seen four lunars of) kind of resist the 'mythical beast' because... very few myths really 'exist' about these animals. In which case, make one up, duh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T04:03:23-07:00","id":926973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926457#post926457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so what are Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div> This question doesn't really refute my point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T04:25:08-07:00","id":926982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926728#post926728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, the next sermon my Zenith tells is going to be The Parable of the Shrimp and the Lobster. It's coalescing as I type.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T04:43:02-07:00","id":926990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926621#post926621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd draw the line here:<br /> <br /> If the mythical animal at one point has a stable breeding population (like huge flying hawks), then it isn't a mythical animal in Creation. Go for it, Lunar.<br /> <br /> If the mythical animal is considered a spiritual entity (like dragons) or requires a Sorcererous working to create, then it isn't a valid Lunar Totem. A lunar would need special knacks/charms to take that animal's form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I mean the cultural value and symbolism of animal in myth when I used the word &quot;Mythological beast&quot;, like bat being a sign of good luck, or the yuan yang bird being a symbol of loyalty and fidelity.<br /> <br /> Since most of the animals in this thread focus on the scientific and biological aspects which are just weird to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T07:09:26-07:00","id":927028,"title":"","content":"I think the focus on physiological aspects of totem animals comes from the much-discussed heartblood transformation, which is entirely about the physical transformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T07:13:35-07:00","id":927031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926990#post926990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I mean the cultural value and symbolism of animal in myth when I used the word &quot;Mythological beast&quot;, like bat being a sign of good luck, or the yuan yang bird being a symbol of loyalty and fidelity.<br /> <br /> Since most of the animals in this thread focus on the scientific and biological aspects which are just weird to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's probably because a lot of animals have really cool biological aspects to them that may be fun to play with in an RPG setting. When looking for uncommon Lunar totems, some people avoid the more common animals with mythological symbolism and look for the weird animals that science just discovered in the past century. <br /> <br /> Though ants are a symbol of hard work from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ant_and_the_Grasshopper\" target=\"_blank\">Aesop's Fables</a>. So sometimes the mythological symbolism and the biological aspects are one in the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T08:23:45-07:00","id":927079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926990#post926990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I mean the cultural value and symbolism of animal in myth when I used the word &quot;Mythological beast&quot;, like bat being a sign of good luck, or the yuan yang bird being a symbol of loyalty and fidelity.<br /> <br /> Since most of the animals in this thread focus on the scientific and biological aspects which are just weird to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game that Lunar inspiration seeds came from was fond of mixing myth and science together, constantly. This thread is kind of low key in comparison. Also, growing a gigantic pistol shrimp claw on one hand makes for a nice answer to the old 1e Alchemicals Siege Devastator submodule of Essence Pulse Cannon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T11:57:57-07:00","id":927211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926066#post926066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's &quot;generic&quot; about an albatross?!?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sparrow, raiton, and other more 'generic' bird totems picked purely so your warform has an excuse to have those super hand wing mutations. Albatross is fine. Its the many Lunar players I've come across who go like &quot;my totem is a wolf, because my character is a brooding loner&quot; or &quot;my totem is a yeddim because super tough so I can't die in combat&quot; - that's the kind of no-effort no-imagination totems I don't like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T12:56:08-07:00","id":927240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926728#post926728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All three of these lunars are still a Bear Totem lunar. But all three have their own myths and legends about what a Bear is. The same can be done for many animals, though 'weirder' and more 'modern' animals (such as the ever popular pistol shrimp, which I've seen four lunars of) kind of resist the 'mythical beast' because... very few myths really 'exist' about these animals. In which case, make one up, duh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! Like ants being a symbol of hard work (already the case IRL) and slavery or farming in a region where ants do these things. Or dolphins seen as a bad omen because of the horrible things fishermen report to have seen them do while smiling. Or anything you can get away with with Lore, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T13:26:30-07:00","id":927253,"title":"","content":"Even though dolphins have been seen both a guardians/saviours in Greek mythology but nasty little fair-folk tricksters by Amazonian tribes. In Arthurian myth, Sir Yvain both has a lion as a companion and has to fight one in his quests, the first representing the virtues of a christian knight and the 2nd representing the dark animalistic impulses of sin.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is that an animal can have many different interpretations in mythology and different cultures. If you want a particular totem to represent something beyond it's natural characteristics, it should be an option that the player and storyteller can work on together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T23:59:11-07:00","id":927471,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking. And personally I have no problem with lunars being the animal planet heroes. I'm not saying they should be like that either. I'm just saying that at this point I don't care how they are &quot;defined&quot; as long as their Charms are cool in this edition. It seems like every lunar fan has his own vision of what they should be. So it's kinda impossible to please all of them. I can make them whatever I like in my games, as long as they give me good rules and magics to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T01:02:27-07:00","id":927482,"title":"","content":"Personal favorites:<ul><li>Jellyfish/Man-o-War</li> <li>Robber Crab, for those tanky ninjas</li> <li>Moa/Maribu Stork, because its always fun to look fabulous while literally kicking the tar out of anyone that gets in the way. See also peacock and pheasant</li> <li>Hippopotamus, for the same reasons.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T08:29:01-07:00","id":927629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=926573#post926573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to see someone play a Lunar with a Pacman Toad as a totem. Being able to swallow things equal to nearly 50% of their body mass and dimensions would be amusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as you're not using it to vicariously play out a weird fetish. <br /> <br /> I would apply this caveat to most totems, for the record. And character concepts for tabletop RPGs in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 