Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as you're not using it to vicariously play out a weird fetish.<br /> <br /> I would apply this caveat to most totems, for the record. And character concepts for tabletop RPGs in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, fine. You're no fun.<br /> <br /> *sets fire to mysterious sexy Sidereal NPC character sheets*<br /> <br /> (But in all seriousness, you are right to keep the creepy away from the game table.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 07-07-2016, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T09:30:23-07:00","id":927648,"title":"","content":"FWIW, I'm more interested in Mythological Beast Lunars rather than Animal Planet Lunars.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say that the latter has no value--I find animal science facts fascinating--but <i>for my understanding </i>of what Lunars are and what Exalted is, etc, myth-beasts are squarely the better fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T09:51:19-07:00","id":927655,"title":"","content":"I think there's a way to have both. And that's to invent mythological trappings for your weird animals.<br /> <br /> The pistol shrimp can cut glass with its strike because it was she who first struck the anathema and their demon gods in the name of Danaa'd, and they embody speed, courage, fearlessness, and martial arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T10:29:36-07:00","id":927674,"title":"","content":"In ages past a vast and terrible Kraken emerged from the depths of the Underworld and began to make war against the living. Luna (or Danaa'd or the Ocean Father or sometimes another god depending on who is telling the story) blessed the pistol shrimps and gave them the power to drive it back. The sparks and flashes of light they give off when attacking are actually blasts of Essence which allow their attacks to strike ghosts and other immaterial beings. To this day in the West, the pistol shrimp is viewed as an enemy of ghosts and protector of the living, and their claws make for popular wards among those who live close to shadowlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T18:01:20-07:00","id":927874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=927629#post927629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as you're not using it to vicariously play out a weird fetish.<br /> <br /> I would apply this caveat to most totems, for the record. And character concepts for tabletop RPGs in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>LoL, honestly I never even considered that type of angle. I just thought it would be amusing to see the faces of a Wyld Hunt when the Lunar Anathema rages into it's war-form, snatches up their leader, and swallows him! It would be priceless!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T04:33:02-07:00","id":931922,"title":"","content":"Ants.<br /> Some people in the East build their villages around anthills, symbol of civilization and community, Some, instead, destroy them whenever they see them within the town's walls; they've seen monstrous-jawed ants assault their neighbours and bring back their eggs, raising them into loyal slaves. The most observant of those villagers noted that the slaver ants, however fearsome, are unable to eat on their own due to the huge weapons replacing their jaws, hence relying on external help to survive, but this does little to diffuse the specter of slavers.<br /> <br /> Mycea leads his men with an iron fist, of which he doesn't have any. Luna's mark comes in the form of stubby insectile claws, sometimes hidden beneath long sleeves, clumsy for any task that doesn't require violence. But this has never stopped him.<br /> He sees the free men from beyond the Treshold, and shakes his head at their weakness, at their refusal to learn and adapt. He sees the Guild, and laughs at their feeble concerns; useless money, debilitating drugs. They do not even employ their slaves efficiently.<br /> Mycea, though considered a barbarian by some, has mastered agriculture and animal husbandry. These symbiotic relations turn plants, animals and people into more than the sum of their parts. Yet, it is only one form of slavery. The so-called society defines slavery as forced unpaid work. Does that makes whatever he practices slavery? Maybe. Does that make the entirety of life slavery? Absolutely. Survival is harsh work, and those who believe themselves free are only fooling themselve.<br /> A few men under his orders are here to help Mycea feed himself, compensating for his lack of dexterous hands. Dignity doesn't enter the equation, never has. Could he starve if they decided to stop feeding him? Sure. But it would take long, way too long, and he knows several ways to kill them, again and again, painfully, before his body even starts begging for sustenance.<br /> Civilization is a matter of specialty. Each one ought to do their part, without expecting reward, for that is a downfall of the so-called &quot;civilized&quot;: entitlement. Some are born to be warriors, some are born to be farmers, some are born to be diplomats. The children who were raised under his rule know all this. They shall help redefine society in a way that befits the reality of the world.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, Mycea shall visit the village of Longmonsoon. They've not been irreversibly tainted by the ways of the Guild or the Realm, he hopes. They cultivate orchards with great skill. Such a loss would it be if they refused his ways. At least, some of their children have already started learning such techniques. Meanwhile, he will keep leading his growing clan, and protect them from the greatest menaces, and keep studying the wise ways of the ancient ants.<br /> <br /> Adaptation, sometimes, is specialization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T18:31:22-07:00","id":934842,"title":"","content":"I cannot recall what kinds of restrictions are placed on Lunars receiving the spirit shapes of animals that are extinct.<br /> <br /> \u200bSuch animals would be uncommon as a matter of course, but I also thought there might be something interesting to the image of a Lunar possessing the form of an animal that was driven to extinction on account of the decadence of the Scarlet Dynasty, whether it be for fur, flesh, or other parts.<br /> <br /> I have this image of a Lunar who can turn into a sturgeon that has been rendered extinct by the Dynasty's taste for caviar, which is not only a little thumbing of the nose towards the sworn enemes of the Lunar Exalted, but also has a mild bit of tension arising from a few Dynast gourmet's who will pay handsomely for anybody who can acquire that Lunar and determine a way to keep her in that shape while the caviar is being extracted anew.<br /> <br /> Or a Lunar who can turn into a setting equivalent of the ortolan bunting running afoul of a standing reward to find a last example of the extinct bird and bring it alive to be drowned in liqeuor, roasted, and consumed whole.<br /> <br /> I cannot recall, if Lunars are killed in their totem shape, do they turn back into a human, or remain in that form? It would make things easier if the former.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T20:01:17-07:00","id":934864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=927674#post927674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In ages past a vast and terrible Kraken emerged from the depths of the Underworld and began to make war against the living. Luna (or Danaa'd or the Ocean Father or sometimes another god depending on who is telling the story) blessed the pistol shrimps and gave them the power to drive it back. The sparks and flashes of light they give off when attacking are actually blasts of Essence which allow their attacks to strike ghosts and other immaterial beings. To this day in the West, the pistol shrimp is viewed as an enemy of ghosts and protector of the living, and their claws make for popular wards among those who live close to shadowlands.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the point that in the West, some refer to Righteous Devil Style as Sparking Claw Style to honor the similarities between the small spectre-hunters of the sea and the brave firedust-slingers who hunt down and sear out evil.<br /> <br /> Let me try my hand at one...<br /> <br /> The cone snail is an example of great beauty coming hand-in-hand with horrifying danger. Many of these largeish snails have beautiful shells; smaller ones are commonly worn whole and polished as pendants, some are ground to make the finest pigments, and some larger ones' shells are carefully cut up and made into beads and ornaments; Western nobility often wear them, taking pride in the necessary irregularity of each piece of shell---every cone-shell ornament is beautifully unique.<br /> At the same time, the snail itself is dangerous beyond imagination. They hunt with a biological poison dart packed with one of the deadliest mundane venoms in all Creation; this makes collecting their shells dangerous, which further increases their value as the demand always far outstrips the supply. Those who watch the snails hunt also recognize their natural danger to other animals; lacking speed, they creep up on unwary fish or hide in the sand, stealthily sliding out to strike and drag the fast-fading goby or other unfortunate fish into the all-too-sudden gaping cavern of a mouth. They swallow their prey whole and move on.<br /> The cone snail is thus both a symbol of beauty and wealth, and of the assassin---both because they themselves are assassins within nature who leave no trace of their victims, and because their venom is dearly prized by killers for their poison darts and needles. Lunars under this totem often hide their deadliness behind facades of opulent beauty, walking as assassins hidden in plain sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T16:57:47-07:00","id":935365,"title":"","content":"has anyone mentioned furnace rhinos yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1044-veritas1980","name":"Veritas1980","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1044_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":4,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T18:43:18-07:00","id":935410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veritas1980</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=935365#post935365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">has anyone mentioned furnace rhinos yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're too inherently magical on their own. Okaying it would be akin to enabling the Unending Celestial Wine Fountain of 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T19:02:58-07:00","id":935413,"title":"","content":"They were given as an example in the sidebar for the Heart's Blood Background in Manual: Lunars, mind.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnyway, I found that Lunars do indeed revert to the last true form they assumed when they die, so it is perfectly viable to slay a Lunar whose totem is a delectable or decorative animal and then using it to engage in a long-forgotten indulgence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T21:19:59-07:00","id":935446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=935413#post935413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were given as an example in the sidebar for the Heart's Blood Background in Manual: Lunars, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's MoEP: Lunars, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T11:03:17-07:00","id":935689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/925797-uncommon-lunar-totems?p=935410#post935410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're too inherently magical on their own. Okaying it would be akin to enabling the Unending Celestial Wine Fountain of 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With that being said, can I have a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pixiu\" target=\"_blank\">Pixiu</a>? It's a gold eating lion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-